  "section_notes": "S1 is fully protective: all thermal incidents (not just confirmed ones) must be reported, 24h for serious and 5 business days for others, with customer notice within 24 hours of a determination that action is needed and no phase-in. S2 keeps the 55 °C / 5% benchmark and gives purchasers the model's results (regulators get data, general public does not), but an over-limit model is not barred from sale while the regulator reviews a corrective-action plan, and no interim cap or sales-stop deadline is set. S3 requires shut-off on new units at 12 months and retrofit of installed units within six years 'where technically feasible' (with owner notification/regulator reporting as the alternative), S4 mandates built-in suppression at 36 months, and S5 keeps a mandatory numeric recall at >8 per 100k with no phase-in but only 'promptly' notices and no serious-injury clause."
